17	 //!
18	 //! AG-UI permits a single active tool call at a time, but core's `ToolCallDelta`s for
19	 //! different ids may interleave freely (`paigasus-helikon-core/src/model.rs:56`) and
20	 //! its `ToolCallItem`s carry no ordering guarantee. Reconciling the two is what
21	 //! [`EventMapper`]'s tool-call state exists for, and it owes an AG-UI client three
22	 //! things: spans never overlap, one call id maps to exactly one span, and an id's
23	 //! args reach the client in receipt order inside that span (a client concatenating
24	 //! `TOOL_CALL_ARGS` deltas would otherwise rebuild malformed JSON). Deltas for an id
25	 //! that arrive while another call holds the span are therefore buffered, not
26	 //! interleaved, and replayed when that id takes the span or is flushed.
27	+//!
28	+//! # Call occurrences
29	+//!
30	+//! Provider call ids are unique **at item level** in one model stream (core's
31	+//! accumulator merges deltas by id), but not across a run: Gemini numbers its calls
32	+//! `fc_{n}` per response, so a later turn, or a handoff child, can reuse an id for a
33	+//! different call. The mapper therefore keys its per-call state on the **AG-UI id**
34	+//! of a call occurrence, not on the provider id. A new occurrence of provider id `x`
35	+//! starts only when the events prove that a new call started: a name-carrying
36	+//! `ToolCallDelta` for `x` when the current occurrence already had one (core gives
37	+//! `name: Some` exactly once per call) or already had its item (an item-only call,
38	+//! then a streamed call that reuses `x`), a `ToolCallItem` for `x` when the current
39	+//! occurrence already had its item, or the first event for `x`. There is no reset at
40	+//! `TurnStarted`: under `ParallelAgent` a sibling's `TurnStarted` can arrive between
41	+//! one call's deltas and its item. The first occurrence of `x` keeps the id `x`; a
42	+//! later one gets `x~n`, with the smallest `n` ≥ 2 that the run has not emitted yet,
43	+//! so an alias never equals a provider id of the run. Every frame of the call
44	+//! (`START`, `ARGS`, `END`, `RESULT`) and the `call_id` of a `helikon.approval` frame
45	+//! use that AG-UI id. AG-UI ids are unique per run only: each request gets a new
46	+//! mapper.
